# Normalisation rules for the Mova Store repository.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git classify a path before any end-of-line conversion runs, so
# an asset that Git recognises as binary is stored byte-for-byte. The explicit
# `binary` rules below then pin every asset type this repository ships, which
# keeps them out of text handling even if a future file defeats the heuristic.
# `eol=lf` is safe to apply repository-wide because it now only takes effect for
# paths Git has already classified as text.
#
# This file used to contain `* text eol=lf`, which forced every path - assets in
# `public/` included - through EOL normalisation, leaving the whole asset set
# reported as modified. After this change lands, run `git add --renormalize .`
# once to refresh the index so a fresh checkout is clean.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Images - never diffed, merged or EOL-converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.bmp binary
*.tiff binary

# Video and audio.
*.mp4 binary
*.m4v binary
*.mov binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary

# Fonts.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary

# Archives and compiled artefacts.
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll binary
